IMPORT prelude

-- Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967 (Singapore) -- collective ("en bloc") sale of a strata development under s 84A, and the
-- bar on adverse possession of common property (s 28).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LTSA1967.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 24 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the collective sale, which is
-- where a strata owner meets the Act. Not encoded: subdivision and the subsidiary strata land-register (Part 2), statutory
-- easements and common property dealings (Part 3) except s 28, termination of schemes (Part 5), the other collective-sale
-- routes (ss 84D to 84FB), Part 8, and the First to Fourth Schedules (procedure, meetings, the committee, deductions).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967 -- collective sale`

§§ `84A(1) -- the majority needed`

-- s 84A(1): an application may be made by subsidiary proprietors with "not less than 90% of the share values AND not less
-- than 90% of the total area of all the lots" where LESS than 10 years have passed since the latest TOP (or CSC if no TOP),
-- or "not less than 80%" of both where 10 YEARS OR MORE have passed.
-- Both tests -- share value and area -- must be met.
DECLARE Consent HAS
    `share value consenting, percent` IS A NUMBER
    `area consenting, percent` IS A NUMBER
    `years since the latest TOP or CSC` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold percent` MEANS
    IF `the consent`'s `years since the latest TOP or CSC` LESS THAN 10 THEN 90 ELSE 80

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the majority may apply for a collective sale` IF
        `the consent`'s `share value consenting, percent` AT LEAST `the threshold percent` `the consent`
    AND `the consent`'s `area consenting, percent` AT LEAST `the threshold percent` `the consent`

§§ `84A(4), (6), (6A), (2A), (2B) -- objections, the Board, and the Court`

-- (4): a non-consenting owner, or a mortgagee or chargee on the register, may object within 21 days of the notice.
-- (6): if no objection, the Board "MUST ... approve" (subject to (9)).
-- (6A): if objections, the Board must mediate; if any objection is not withdrawn after 60 days of mediation (or when
-- mediation has gone as far as it can), the Board "must ... order a discontinuance" -- a "stop order" (after 7 days' notice,
-- (6B)).
-- (2A), (2B): the application may then go to the High Court, but ONLY after a stop order and within 14 DAYS of it.
DECLARE Route HAS
    `objections filed` IS A NUMBER
    `objections withdrawn after mediation` IS A NUMBER
    `days since the stop order` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board must approve without a hearing of objections` IF
    `the route`'s `objections filed` EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board must issue a stop order` IF
    `the route`'s `objections filed` GREATER THAN `the route`'s `objections withdrawn after mediation`

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicants may go to the High Court` IF
        `the Board must issue a stop order` `the route`
    AND `the route`'s `days since the stop order` AT MOST 14

§§ `84A(7), (8) -- the objector's two grounds`

-- (7): the High Court "is to ... approve ... UNLESS" satisfied that "(a) any objector, being a subsidiary proprietor, will
-- incur a FINANCIAL LOSS; or (b) the proceeds of sale for any lot ... are INSUFFICIENT TO REDEEM ANY MORTGAGE or charge".
-- (8): a financial loss means (a) proceeds, after allowed deductions, "LESS THAN THE PRICE ... PAID for that lot"; (b) NOT
-- "by reason only that the ... net gain ... will be LESS THAN THE OTHER subsidiary proprietors"; (c) NOT where the owner
-- "PURCHASED THE LOT AFTER a collective sale committee had signed a sale and purchase agreement".
--
-- The objector's grounds are narrow. Receiving less than one's neighbours is not a loss; receiving less than market value is
-- not a loss; only receiving less than one paid is. A buyer who bought after the committee signed has no loss ground at all.
DECLARE Objector HAS
    `net proceeds after deductions` IS A NUMBER
    `price paid for the lot` IS A NUMBER
    `outstanding mortgage` IS A NUMBER
    `bought after the committee signed the sale agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the objector` IS AN Objector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objector incurs a financial loss` IF
        `the objector`'s `net proceeds after deductions` LESS THAN `the objector`'s `price paid for the lot`
    AND NOT `the objector`'s `bought after the committee signed the sale agreement`

GIVEN `the objector` IS AN Objector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeds cannot redeem the mortgage` IF
    `the objector`'s `net proceeds after deductions` LESS THAN `the objector`'s `outstanding mortgage`

GIVEN `the objector` IS AN Objector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection defeats the sale` IF
        `the objector incurs a financial loss` `the objector`
    OR  `the proceeds cannot redeem the mortgage` `the objector`

GIVEN `my gain` IS A NUMBER, `neighbours' average gain` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a smaller gain than neighbours is a financial loss` IF
    FALSE

§§ `84A(7A), (7B) -- topping up objectors`

-- (7A): with the collective sale committee's consent, the Court may increase an objector's proceeds if just and equitable.
-- (7B): "The total sum ordered ... for ALL the objectors ... must not exceed the aggregate sum of 0.25% of the proceeds of
-- sale for each lot or $2,000 for each lot, whichever is the higher."
-- (9)(b): and if the committee does not consent to such an order, the sale cannot be approved.
--
-- Read per lot: the cap is, for each lot in the development, the higher of 0.25% of that lot's proceeds or $2,000, summed.
-- The text could also be read with "whichever is the higher" applied to the two aggregates; the per-lot reading is encoded.
GIVEN `lot proceeds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cap contribution of one lot` MEANS
    IF `lot proceeds` TIMES 0.0025 GREATER THAN 2000 THEN `lot proceeds` TIMES 0.0025 ELSE 2000

GIVEN `number of lots` IS A NUMBER, `proceeds per lot` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cap on top-ups for a uniform development` MEANS
    `number of lots` TIMES `the cap contribution of one lot` `proceeds per lot`

§§ `84A(9) -- good faith`

-- (9)(a)(i): the Court or Board must not approve if satisfied the transaction is not in good faith "after taking into
-- account ONLY the following factors: (A) the sale price ...; (B) the method of distributing the proceeds ...; and (C) the
-- relationship of the purchaser to any of the subsidiary proprietors". (ii): nor if non-consenting owners would have to join
-- any development arrangement.
--
-- "Only": a committee's conduct of the sale, its conflicts, and the process are not factors under (9)(a)(i) unless they bear on
-- price, distribution or the purchaser's relationship.
DECLARE Factor IS ONE OF
    `the sale price`
    `the method of distribution`
    `the purchaser's relationship to an owner`
    `the committee's conduct of the process`
    `the timing of the sale in the market cycle`

GIVEN `the factor` IS A Factor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the factor counts for good faith under section 84A(9)(a)(i)` IF
    CONSIDER `the factor`
    WHEN `the sale price` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the method of distribution` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the purchaser's relationship to an owner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `28 -- no squatting on common property`

-- s 28: "No action shall be brought by any person claiming title by adverse possession to the common property of a parcel or
-- to any accessory lot", and the Limitation Act's adverse-possession provisions do not extend to it.
GIVEN `years of exclusive use of common property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `adverse possession can give title to the common property` IF
    FALSE
